Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: determine AP mode before direct association

FT over DS reaches association without a preceding authentication request.
In this case the connection settings have only been limited by local
capabilities when the AP HT/VHT capability elements are read. A VHT-capable
station therefore rejects a valid 5 GHz HT-only AP before prep_connection()
can derive the AP mode.

Use the existing channel preparation helper in calculation-only mode for
unmatched non-MLO association before extracting the HT/VHT elements. Keep
local request restrictions, AP membership and channel checks, and leave the
actual channel/station acquisition and its cleanup in prep_connection().
Matching authentication and MLO paths are unchanged.

--- a/net/mac80211/mlme.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/mlme.c
@@ -10480,6 +10480,20 @@
 
 		uapsd_supported = bss->uapsd_supported;
 
+		/*
+		 * Direct association (e.g. FT over DS) has no authentication
+		 * step to limit the connection mode to the target AP. Do that
+		 * before requiring the mode-specific capability elements.
+		 * A NULL link only calculates the mode, without using a channel.
+		 */
+		if (!match_auth) {
+			err = ieee80211_prep_channel(sdata, NULL, NULL, 0, cbss,
+						     false, &assoc_data->link[0].conn,
+						     sdata->u.mgd.userspace_selectors);
+			if (err)
+				goto err_free;
+		}
+
 		err = ieee80211_mgd_get_ap_ht_vht_capa(sdata, assoc_data, 0);
 		if (err)
 			goto err_free;
